iving in fear and did the  optics include that it might be  perceived  as an attempt to divert  attention from the responsibility of the  rcmp for  what had happened on the  the night of the murders no  that that actually never crossed my mind  banfield's charges were eventually moved  from the courts to restorative justice  she's been discharged with no criminal  record  ross lord global news  the campaign to free brittany griner  ahead the legal battle to prove russia  wrongfully detained the american  basketball star  global national is back from edmonton  after this  [Music]  welcome back to edmonton now to  washington where former u.s president  donald trump returned for the first time  since leaving office  we have become a beggar nation groveling  to other countries for energy  millions of illegal aliens are  stampeding across our wide open borders  pouring into our country it's an  invasion  democrat-run cities are setting all time  trump is being advised to speak more  about his vision for the future and less  about the 2020 election that he claims  was stolen by joe biden  today trump made his case for a possible  second term ahead of the november  midterm election saying america is  facing an energy crunch fueled by  democrat policies  european union member states agreed on a  plan to reduce natural gas consumption  as russia cut supply and the war in  ukraine shows no end in sight the bloc  agreed to temporarily lower demand for  natural gas by 15 percent but says the  move may become mandatory if russia  turns off the taps completely and  storage levels drop dramatically the  deal was reached a day after russian  energy giant gazprom announced it was  cutting daily gas deliveries to germany  in half from 40 percent down to 20  percent  american basketball star brittany griner  appeared in a russian court today her  fifth hearing after being arrested in  february over cannabis oil found in her  luggage her defense team focused on  testimony from a narcol